  "notes": "USAGE:\n{夕暮|ゆうぐ}れ{時|どき} is a common compound meaning \"at twilight/dusk.\"\n{夕暮|ゆうぐ}れ has a poetic, atmospheric quality often associated with nostalgia or melancholy in Japanese literature and art.\n\nRELATED TIME EXPRESSIONS:\n- {夕方|ゆうがた} - evening (broader term, more commonly used)\n- {日暮|ひぐ}れ - sunset, nightfall\n- {黄昏|たそがれ} - twilight (more literary)\n- {暁|あかつき} - dawn (opposite time)",
